The Android app contains NetBird's client library (lib/arm64-v8a/libgojni.so
and the Java bindings in io.netbird.gomobile), built by android/netbird from
https://github.com/netbirdio/netbird at tag v0.83.1, package client/android.
Only the client is used: nothing from NetBird's management/, signal/, relay/
or combined/ directories (AGPL-3.0) is built into it. NetBird's Android app
(netbirdio/android-client, GPL-3.0) is not used; the app's NetBird glue
(android/src/at/quickme/prism/netbird) is this repository's own.

The library also links the Go standard library and Go modules named in
NetBird's go.mod at that tag, each under its own licence (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0,
and MPL-2.0 for github.com/hashicorp/errwrap, go-multierror and go-version,
whose sources are available from their repositories unchanged).

